      "text": "To determine the volume of the frustum, we first need to calculate the volumes of both the original pyramid and the smaller pyramid with the cut. The volume \\( V \\) of a pyramid is given by the formula:\n\n\\[\nV = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\text{Base Area} \\times \\text{Height}\n\\]\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the volume of the original pyramid.**\n\nThe base of the original pyramid is a square with a side length of 12 cm.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Base Area} = 12 \\times 12 = 144 \\text{ cm}^2\n\\]\n\\[\nV_{\\text{original}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 \\times 8 = 408 \\text{ cm}^3\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the volume of the smaller pyramid.**\n\nThe base of the smaller pyramid is a square with a side length of 6 cm.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Base Area} = 6 \\times 6 = 36 \\text{ cm}^2\n\\]\n\\[\nV_{\\text{smaller}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 36 \\times 4 = 48 \\text{ cm}^3\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the volume of the frustum.**\n\nThe volume of the frustum is the volume of the original pyramid minus the volume of the smaller pyramid.\n\n\\[\nV_{\\text{frustum}} = V_{\\text{original}} - V_{\\text{smaller}} = 408 - 48 = 360 \\text{ cm}^3\n\\]\n\nThus, the volume of the frustum is \\(\\boxed{360}\\) cubic centimeters.",
